                0.15,
                0.923,
                0.226
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "intensifying competition in the NEV segment, scale benefits, pricing actions, and portfolio diversification are expected to support a more stable margin profile over the medium term. The company cited a strong demand outlook driven by Semi, CNC, and machine tools, with machine tools seeing meaningful spillover demand from AI data center buildout (cooling and aluminum/metal processing), in addition to strong semi industry demand, positioning 2026 as another upcycle year with pricing increases of (5-20%) to offset cost inflation.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "bbox": [
                0.069,
                0.241,
                0.666,
                0.258
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "EXPORT CHAMPIONS - Auto Parts, Power Equipment & Construction Machinery"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.068,
                0.271,
                0.922,
                0.528
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Attended meetings with Sany Heavy (600031 CH/6031 HK), Fuyao Glass (3606 HK), and Huaming Power (002270 CH), where investors' key questions centered on overseas market expansion and global competitive dynamics. Sany highlighted resilient growth momentum despite FX and relatively weaker financing capabilities compared to global peers (CAT US, Komatsu in JP), underpinned by strong competitiveness in sub-100 tonne excavators and accelerating overseas expansion, particularly in Africa, Latin America, and Southeast Asia. While technology gaps and financing persist in ultra-large equipment and developed markets, management emphasizes disciplined growth, improving service capability, and a favorable replacement cycle in domestic China to sustain above-industry growth without compromising profitability or cash flow. Huaming highlighted its technology and cost leadership in the global tap changer market, set to benefit from high entry barriers and growing global customer demand for dual sourcing away from MR (the global market leader, Germany). While domestic China demand is mature, the company focuses on the EU, Turkey, and US markets to drive growth, supported by strong order momentum and long-term electrification demand. Management remains confident in sustaining double-digit growth and expanding global market share over the next few years, despite intensified competitive responses from incumbents. Fuyao Glass highlighted its improving mix toward higher value-added NEV and functional glass, underpinning a sustainable 37–38% GPM outlook (despite cost inflation impact), while strategically positioning itself with a leading US OEM and expanding from side windows into panoramic and sunroof products, with further shipment growth as capacity gradually shifts from China to overseas. Competitive dynamics are favorable as Japanese peers face capacity and raw material constraints, while EU suppliers are pressured by higher energy and labor costs, supporting further m/s gains in the EU and US.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
